---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="Myursel Shahin — AI student at Radboud University, based in Arnhem."
	pubDate={new Date('September 09 2026')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
		I'm Myursel — an Artificial Intelligence student at Radboud University in Nijmegen, currently in
		my third year and living in Arnhem.
	</p>

	<h2>How I got here</h2>

	<p>
		I grew up in Izmir. I got my first computer at six and started properly messing with logic
		around ten, automating things with Minecraft command blocks, which turned out to be a decent
		introduction to programming. Maths was the subject that stuck — I competed in olympiads in
		middle school — and I went on to Bornova Anadolu Lisesi.
	</p>

	<p>
		After school I spent a year in The Hague working in logistics and delivery, then a stint as a
		coordinator at Rotterdam Fruit Wharf. I moved to Dublin next, where I worked in a kitchen and
		bar at the airport and started a university foundation year that I ultimately decided not to
		finish. That detour is the reason I know what I actually want to study.
	</p>

	<p>
		Since September 2024 I've been at Radboud on the BSc Artificial Intelligence, expecting to
		graduate in 2027. I completed the Radboud Honours Academy's interdisciplinary programme for
		first-year students in 2025, and I'm a member of CognAC, the AI study association.
	</p>

	<h2>What I work on</h2>

	<p>
		Mostly things I can run and see working. A local multimodal AI stack on my own laptop.
		PaperScroll, a Next.js feed that pulls papers from arXiv. A Raspberry Pi handling DNS and DHCP
		for network-level filtering at home, with an automation server planned on top of it. Alongside
		that, coursework in reinforcement learning, Bayesian networks, explainable AI and robotics.
	</p>

	<p>
		I'm heading toward machine learning and data engineering — pipelines, deployment, the parts that
		have to keep running after the notebook closes.
	</p>

	<h2>Away from the screen</h2>

	<p>
		I cook a lot and I'm reasonably serious about it. I shoot photos, which I've been doing since
		the photography club in high school. I listen to records. I work part-time in a kitchen in
		Arnhem, which keeps the week honest.
	</p>

	<h2>Get in touch</h2>

	<p>
		The links in the footer all work — <a href="https://github.com/Myursel777">GitHub</a> for code,
		<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/myursel-shahin/">LinkedIn</a> for the professional version, or
		just email me.
	</p>
</Layout>
